  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>y</mi></math> be real numbers such that <math><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> . If the complex number <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math> satisfies <math><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then which of the following is (are) possible value (s) of <math><mi>x</mi><mo>?</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rSDKx",
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math>",
